# Ship to Git and Vercel

Once a change is implemented, ship it in the same turn. Do not wait to be asked to push.

1. Commit the relevant files (never `.env` or secrets). Follow the repo commit style: one or two sentences on why.
2. `git push origin HEAD` on the current branch (`rebuild/member-app` unless told otherwise).
3. Wait until the new Vercel Preview is Ready, then promote it:

```
npx vercel promote <preview-url> --yes --scope cinnamon-snail
```

Production is https://cinnamon-snail-community.vercel.app. A git push only creates Preview; live traffic needs promote.

Skip this loop only when the user asked for a local-only experiment, or there is nothing to commit.
